    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Khalid al-Rashid was a Muslim warlord during the Crusades whose reputation for atrocity was extreme even by the standards of that brutal age &mdash; a reputation that drew the attention of a Cainite who Embraced him amid the bloodshed of the Holy Land. Khalid went berserk upon realizing what he had become, savaging his own men before fleeing into the desert, where a reclusive Jewish hermit saved him from the sun and sheltered him for a month while he studied Kabbalistic mysticism. That study transformed him. Now resident in Chicago, Khalid is a solitary, mystically inclined Assamite whose Kabbalah-inflected worldview and violent past make him an unpredictable, dangerous factor in the city's Kindred affairs.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Speak rarely, and when you do, invoke scripture and mysticism. Violence is a language you know better than words, but you have learned, painfully, to hold it in check.</p>",
    "notes": "Solitary and unpredictable. Studies Kabbalistic mysticism. A wildcard whose old Crusader violence lurks beneath a veneer of contemplative restraint.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
